[size=5][b]Full Art Spire[/b][/size]
Full-art versions of Slay the Spire 2's cards: all 577 cards of the main game (every character, plus colorless, event, token, curse, status and quest cards) and the Fool's 90 cards from the public beta.

[b]Visual only.[/b] No gameplay or balance changes; the mod is flagged as not affecting gameplay. See interactive previews and the card gallery on the [url=https://tzii.github.io/full-art-spire/]showcase site[/url].

[size=4][b]Features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Full art on every card.[/b] Each portrait is extended to fill the card.
[*][b]Layered depth.[/b] The character stands in front of its background and follows your cursor with gentle parallax, a soft shadow and rim light.
[*][b]Rarity finishes.[/b] Starters and commons get a subtle silver satin, uncommons a pearl holo, rares gold foil with glints and an aura, and Ancient cards a full prismatic finish with a rainbow aura.
[*][b]A switch per pack.[/b] Each character and card type is its own pack. Switch any of them off in the settings and the change shows at once, even on cards already on screen.
[*][b]Smooth loading.[/b] Textures stream in on background threads.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[url=https://www.nexusmods.com/slaythespire2/mods/103]BaseLib[/url] 3.3.0 or newer. It also provides the settings menu.

[size=4][b]Install[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Install BaseLib.
[*]Extract the archive into [i]Slay the Spire 2/mods/[/i], so you get [i]mods/full_art_spire/full_art_spire.json[/i].
[*]Coming from Full Art Card Packs: delete the old [i]mods/full_art_card_packs[/i] folder. Until you do, Full Art Spire stays off and the main menu shows a warning, so the two never change the same cards. Your settings and pack choices carry over.
[*]Start the game and allow mods if asked.
[/list]
To uninstall, delete the [i]full_art_spire[/i] folder. The mod is also on the Steam Workshop, where it updates by itself.

[size=4][b]Settings[/b][/size]
Open the mod settings from the BaseLib menu. You can switch each card pack on or off, turn the finishes off or fade them, switch finish styles, adjust or disable parallax, enable Reduced Motion, or show flat full art without layers. Press [b]F8[/b] while hovering a card to save a local report for bug reports.

[size=4][b]Notes[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Made for Slay the Spire 2 v0.107.1 and the v0.113.1 public beta. Cards added in later updates keep their original art until the mod catches up; on the current beta that is 50 new cards.
[*]The full-art extensions and the depth-layer backgrounds are AI-generated (OpenAI image models), starting from Mega Crit's original card art, and reviewed against it. Some cutouts may show small edge artifacts: please report them with F8 and a screenshot.
[*]The images are re-encoded to save space, which removes the C2PA Content Credentials the image generator embedded.
[*][b]For mod authors:[/b] other mods can ship full art for their own cards. The pack format and its validator are on [url=https://github.com/tzii/full-art-spire]GitHub[/url], with the source code (MIT).
[/list]

Unofficial fan project, not affiliated with or endorsed by Mega Crit. All original Slay the Spire 2 art, characters and designs belong to Mega Crit. BaseLib by Alchyr.
